{
 "about": "Exact 2-SFS class certificates for popcorn.twosfs at n = 3..6 (the same models as support_hull.json plus the constant-size Kingman control at n = 4, 5, 6). witness_W is a rational vector over pairs 'i,j' (i <= j) with max|W_ij| = 1; G_M_lambda_exact = <W, M> = sum_{i<=j} W_ij E[L_i L_j] for the row's model (exact, < 0 in every row); norm_margin_exact = -<W, M>/E[L_tot^2]; delta_l1_lb_exact = norm_margin / max|W_ij|, a certified lower bound on the l1 distance (ordered pairs) between the model's normalized 2-SFS and that of any member of the excluded class; eta is the interior slack that was asked of the proposing LP. verdict OUT_FULLCLASS: K_W(x,y) = sum W_ij Csym_ij(x,y) >= 0 on the unit square is certified by exact tensor-Bernstein subdivision (twosfs_certificates.bern_2d_nonneg), so the model's expected 2-SFS lies outside that of EVERY single-population Kingman coalescent with deterministic size history and every pooling of such histories: all 13 Lambda rows with n >= 4. verdict OUT_ATOMPOOLINGS: only the diagonal p_W(t) = sum W_ij m2_ij(t) >= 0 on [0,1] is certified (bern_1d_nonneg), excluding poolings of single-atom limit histories on any support but not time-varying histories: the three n = 3 rows and the three Kingman controls (full_class_search = no_certified_witness; for the controls no full-class witness can exist). Every certificate was re-derived exactly from these witnesses with the shipped code (twosfs_certificates.certify_witness); the package battery re-certifies all rows with n <= 5 on every run and checks every row's exact margin.",
